{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310683,"nonce":"FckuZTv4li7keQxeuhJEfhsR0eQ=","title":"OPEN — Reflect.field(obj,\\\"method\\\") returns NULL because methods take no field slot, so isFunction is false and Reflect.callMethod calls ...","message":"**REPRO** (`/tmp/cm/C.hx`):\n```haxe\nclass T { public var n = 5; public function new() {} public function add(a:Int,b:Int) return n+a+b; }\nvar f = Reflect.field(t, \"add\");\nReflect.isFunction(f);            // false  (should be true)\nReflect.callMethod(t, f, [1,2]);  // SIGSEGV\n```\n\n**THE CHAIN, measured:**\n1. `haxe_reflect_field` (runtime/src/reflect.rs:130) asks `lookup_class_field`,\n   which only knows SLOTS. A method occupies none ⇒ returns NULL.\n2. `haxe_reflect_is_function` reads `DynamicValue.type_id == TYPE_FUNCTION`;\n   null ⇒ false.\n3. `Reflect.callMethod` is NOT a runtime symbol — despite\n   `runtime_mapping.rs:4204` naming `haxe_reflect_call_method`, which does not\n   exist. The compiler lowers it in `mir/expr/reflect.rs`\n   (`lower_reflect_call_method`): it resolves the callee statically when arg 1\n   is a Variable naming a function, and otherwise CallIndirects the lowered\n   expression — here NULL. **So the blocker is step 1, not callMethod.**\n\n**EIGHT ATTEMPTS, ALL FAILED IDENTICALLY (2026-09-10) — STOP GUESSING.** Registering\nmethod names from `__vtable_init__` always ends in\n`cranelift-jit: can't resolve symbol copy`. Proved it is the loop: gating it\nbehind an env var gives the original behaviour OFF and the panic ON. The\nunresolved symbol is plain `copy` -- the thunk's TARGET, not the thunk -- so\n`ensure_vtable_dispatch_thunk` emits a CallDirect to a function the JIT has no\ncode for. `haxe.ds.BalancedTree` (SymbolId 673: set/get/remove/exists/copy/\nmerge/balance) is the class that trips it.\n\nGuards that did NOT work, in order: (1) vtable-slot loop only -- misses plain\nmethods entirely, since only VIRTUAL methods get a slot and a class with no\nvirtual dispatch has no vtable; (2) every `HirTypeDecl::Class`; (3)\n`module.functions.contains_key(func_id)`; (4) that plus a non-empty CFG;\n(5) `method.function.body.is_some()`; (6) recording at the real lowering site\n(`decl/module.rs`, the non-static `lower_function_body` call) and looking the\nfunction up by NAME -- `find_function_by_name(\"copy\")` binds a NAMESAKE in\nanother module, my own error; (7) the same but keyed by SYMBOL through\n`function_map`, plus a target-has-body check; (8) draining\n`local_instance_methods` per module (IrFunctionId is module-local and the\ncontext is reused across modules) — also no change.\n\n**DO NOT ATTEMPT A NINTH GUARD.** Read the JIT linking model first:\n`cranelift_backend.rs` declares every function in `mir_module.functions`\n(skipping `uses_wide_vectors`), `collect_indirect_targets` (ir/abi.rs) gathers\nFunctionRef/MakeClosure targets AND `__vtable_init__`'s CallDirect targets, and\n`pending_stub_safety_net` trap-stubs bodyless ones. Work out from THAT which\nids a module may legally `build_function_ref`, and why the existing vtable-slot\nloop is safe where this one is not. A different design may be cheaper anyway:\nregister the method WITHOUT emitting a new FunctionRef — e.g. reuse the closure\npointer the vtable loop already builds, or have the runtime resolve the name\nfrom the JIT symbol map.\n\n**COST WARNING: this bug is worth ~8 corpus rows and has now consumed more\neffort than every landed fix of the session combined. Weigh that before\nreturning to it.**\n\n**WHAT THIS MEANS:** knowing the shape of the fix was NOT sufficient -- the\nmissing piece is the JIT's linking model, i.e. which functions a module may\nemit a `build_function_ref` to. Find that rule FIRST (what makes a\n`CallDirect` target resolvable at JIT link time, and how the existing vtable\nloop avoids the problem) before attempting an eighth guard.\n\n**ATTEMPT REVERTED (2026-09-10).** Added `METHOD_REGISTRY` +\n`haxe_register_method_name(type_id, name, closure)` in type_system.rs, a\nmethod fallback in `haxe_reflect_field`, and emission beside\n`haxe_vtable_set_slot` in decl/vtables.rs. **Emitted 30 registrations but did\nNOT fix the repro: only VIRTUALLY DISPATCHED methods get a vtable slot**, and a\nplain class like `T` has no vtable at all (`__vtable_init__` for it registers\nonly its constructor). Widening the loop to every `HirTypeDecl::Class` in\n`current_hir_types` then broke the build outright —\n`cranelift-jit: can't resolve symbol copy` — because it emits dispatch thunks\nfor stdlib methods that are not linked in. Registration must be limited to the\nuser classes actually being compiled, and probably keyed off the same list\nCodex already registers as `ClassInfo.instance_methods` (names are there; the\nPOINTERS are what is missing).\n\nBoxing a found method is easy once the pointer exists:\n`haxe_box_function_ptr(closure)` already tags `TYPE_FUNCTION`.\n\n**SIZE:** 8 corpus tests use `Reflect.callMethod`, all failing (7 CRASH,\n1 WRONG_ANSWER, 1 SKIP). Also blocks `Type.getClassFields` (returns `[]`) and\n`Reflect.isFunction`.\n\nRelated: [[project_haxe_conformance_baseline]] — reflection is the\nhighest-rate cluster (74% of 77 tests) but splits into many small APIs.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_reflect_field_returns_null_for_methods` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}